# Changelog

## FM-DX Console 1.7.0
- Rename the unreleased 1.62.0 build to 1.7.0 for the shared CLI/GUI overhaul; this release follows 1.61.0 chronologically.
- Share the receiver lifecycle, validated tuner actions, history, settings and server filtering between CLI and GUI.
- Share shortcut definitions, tuner profiles, signal conversions, station fields and broadcast/RDS display models.
- Keep transport independent of presentation, with reusable Node-worker and Chromium audio output adapters.
- Fix Electron's renderer startup collision that prevented connecting.
- Add GUI recent-server selection, reconnect handling, bandwidth/AGC, forced stereo, volume and raw-command controls.
- Make Esc return to the startup server selector in both interfaces.
- Handle string-valued tuner flags correctly and retain zero-valued station fields.
- Bound Chromium audio queues and prune old buffered audio between appends.
- Exercise connections, tuning, RDS workers, decoded MP3 audio and switching in packaged GUI smoke tests.

## FM-DX Console 1.61.0
- Package CLI archives with a checksum-verified Node runtime and compiled JSX; no npm installation required.
- Build desktop DMG/ZIP, Windows installer and Linux AppImage/DEB packages using GitHub Actions.
- Publish complete releases only after tests, lint, audit and packaged CLI/GUI smoke checks pass.
- Include release checksums and distinguish installers from GitHub source downloads.
- Fix packaged Electron command-line argument parsing.
- Organize desktop, shared modules, audio and workers under src; move launch helpers into scripts.
- Remove unused legacy audio/antenna helpers, retired Blessed demos and the outdated 1.50 screenshot.
- Choose from the last 25 connected servers at startup or with the m shortcut.
- Keep public-directory browsing and manual URL entry available in the selector.
- Fix disconnect crashes, RDS reconnects, delayed audio exits and invalid frequency input.
- Preserve URL path/query case and discard stale server metadata and commands on switching.
- Validate and atomically persist configuration, with migration of saved last-server settings.
- Remove the unused Android project and build artifacts.
- Update dependencies, require Node.js 22.13 or newer and recommend Node.js 24 LTS.
- Repair Electron CommonJS entry points and enable its default sandbox.
- Add regression tests, linting and a reproducible npm lockfile.

## FM-DX Console 1.52
- Larger pop-up for server information matching the help window
- Redraw screen after closing server info to remove artifacts
- Added 's' shortcut to toggle server info

## FM-DX Console 1.50

- UI Enhancements:
  - Redesigned the help menu into a two-column layout for improved clarity.
  - Made incremental UI improvements for a cleaner and more intuitive experience.
  - Removed unused keys, as cursor navigation now handles these functionalities.

- Performance Improvements:
  - Optimized screen refresh logic for smoother operation.
  - Introduced command throttling to enhance responsiveness and prevent overloading.

- New Features:
  - Introduced dynamic screen functionality, enabling adaptable layouts for improved usability and scalability.

## FM-DX Console 1.41

- Fixed display issues with iMS and EQ when using fm-dx-webserver version 1.2.7.

## FM-DX Console 1.4

- Fixed a crash that occurred when closing the tuning window.
- Added a ping every 5 seconds for more realistic response times.
- Implemented meta property tags for titles and descriptions.
- Redesigned the server information box.
- Moved the connected URL display to the bottom of the window.
- Added buffering during playback to prevent audio artifacts.
- Enhanced URL filtering to support ctrl-fm-tuner.nl URLs.
- Added a default antenna name to avoid an antenna being named 'undefined'.
